---
import {
  ExternalLink,
  GitBranch,
  Monitor,
  Shield,
  Smartphone,
} from "@lucide/astro";
import { DESKTOP_REPO, REPO } from "../../../config/site";
---

<section
  id="beta-updates"
  class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface p-7 md:p-10"
>
  <div
    class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-white/5 px-4 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-vega-accent"
  >
    <GitBranch class="h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true" />
    Beta Updates
  </div>

  <h1
    class="mt-4 font-headline text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,3.1rem)] font-black tracking-tight text-white"
  >
    Opt In to Beta Channel Updates
  </h1>

  <p class="mt-3 max-w-[72ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-vega-muted">
    Test upcoming features and fixes early by switching Vega's update channel to
    Beta, or switch back to Stable whenever you prefer tested releases only.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6 space-y-5">
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <h2 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-white">
        1. Stable vs. Beta Channel
      </h2>
      <ul
        class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2.5 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted marker:text-vega-accent"
      >
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Stable (default):</strong> Checks only the latest
          full public release.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Beta:</strong> Includes both stable releases
          and GitHub prereleases. On Android phones, Beta also includes <strong
            class="text-white">nightly builds</strong
          > (on Android TV, Beta receives stable releases and beta prereleases only,
          since nightly builds target phones).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Back up first:</strong> Beta and nightly builds
          can occasionally introduce regressions. Export a backup before switching
          (<strong class="text-white">Settings &gt; Data management</strong> on
          Android, or <strong class="text-white"
            >Settings &gt; About &gt; Backup</strong
          > on Desktop).
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-white">
        <Smartphone class="h-5 w-5 text-vega-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
        <h2 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold">
          2. Opt In on Android &amp; Android TV (GitHub Build)
        </h2>
      </div>
      <ol
        class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-2.5 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted marker:text-vega-accent"
      >
        <li>
          Make sure you are running the <strong class="text-white"
            >GitHub APK build</strong
          >. Google Play Store builds receive updates through the Play Store and
          hide in-app update controls.
        </li>
        <li>
          Open <strong class="text-white"
            >Settings &gt; About &amp; updates</strong
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          Tap <strong class="text-white">Update channel</strong> and select <strong
            class="text-white">Beta</strong
          > (<em class="text-white/90">Receive stable releases and prereleases</em
          >).
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="text-vega-muted"
            >(Optional) Keep <strong class="text-white"
              >Check on startup</strong
            > and <strong class="text-white">Download updates in Vega</strong> enabled
            so updates prompt and download inside the app.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          Tap <strong class="text-white">Check for updates</strong> to pull the newest
          matching release immediately. When installing an update for the first time,
          grant <strong class="text-white">Install unknown apps</strong> permission
          for Vega in Android settings, then tap <strong class="text-white"
            >Install</strong
          >.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-white">
        <Shield class="h-5 w-5 text-vega-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
        <h2 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold">
          3. Switching Back to Stable
        </h2>
      </div>
      <ul
        class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2.5 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted marker:text-vega-accent"
      >
        <li>
          Go to <strong class="text-white"
            >Settings &gt; About &amp; updates &gt; Update channel</strong
          > and choose <strong class="text-white">Stable</strong>. Vega will
          stay on your installed build until a newer stable release has a higher
          version number.
        </li>
        <li>
          To downgrade immediately, export a backup in <strong
            class="text-white">Settings &gt; Data management</strong
          >, uninstall the beta build, install the latest stable APK from GitHub
          Releases, and restore your backup.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-vega-surface-hi p-5">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-white">
        <Monitor class="h-5 w-5 text-vega-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
        <h2 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold">
          4. Desktop &amp; Store Builds
        </h2>
      </div>
      <ul
        class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2.5 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-vega-muted marker:text-vega-accent"
      >
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Store builds:</strong> Google Play Store (Android)
          and Microsoft Store (Windows) manage updates through their stores and do
          not include an in-app Beta channel switch.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Vega Desktop (GitHub build):</strong> The
          in-app updater (<strong class="text-white"
            >Settings &gt; About &gt; Check for Updates</strong
          >) tracks stable releases. When desktop prereleases are published, you
          can download and install them manually from GitHub Releases.
        </li>
        <li>
          Found an issue in a beta or nightly build? Follow the{" "}
          <a
            class="font-bold text-vega-accent underline underline-offset-4"
            href="/guide/report-bugs">Report Bugs &amp; Logs guide</a
          >{" "}
          so we can fix it before the next stable release.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-vega-accent px-4 py-2 text-sm font-bold text-[#240900] transition hover:-translate-y-0.5"
          href={REPO.releasesUrl}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          <ExternalLink class="h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true" />
          Android/TV Releases
        </a>
        <a
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-bold text-white transition hover:bg-white/12"
          href={DESKTOP_REPO.releasesUrl}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          <ExternalLink class="h-4 w-4 text-vega-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
          Desktop Releases
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
